<section id="purpose"><div class="wrap split">
 <div><span class="label eyebrow muted">Purpose</span><h2 class="disp">Why we exist.</h2></div>
 <div class="prose"><p class="pull" style="margin-bottom:24px">To make furniture that lasts a long time.</p>
 <p>Hotels and restaurants spend years building a sense of place, and many of them look to Danish design for credibility. Then they furnish those places with pieces that won't last: plastic chairs and loungers that are bought, worn out and replaced on a short cycle.</p>
 <p>That gap is the reason Another Life exists. We make furniture that earns the design it borrows from: well made, built from material that already exists, and designed to be repaired rather than thrown away.</p>
 <p>The new luxury is longevity.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section id="design"><div class="wrap split">
 <div><span class="label eyebrow muted">Design principles</span><h2 class="disp">Danish design, made where the material is.</h2>
 <p class="prose" style="margin-top:24px">Our design follows a Scandinavian tradition: simple, functional, made to last and to never go out of style. The pieces are made by hand in Indonesia, close to the timber and the people who work it.</p><div class="lead-img"><figure class="fig"><img src="{{ 'design-table-sun.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A dark timber table in afternoon sun with chair drawings, a sketchbook, a laptop showing chair designs, a burned teak sample and two coffee cups" width="768" height="1024" loading="lazy"><figcaption class="cap">Sketches, drawings and a burned sample on the design table.</figcaption></figure></div></div>
 <div class="rows"><div class="row"><h3 class="disp">Knock-down</h3><p>Every piece ships disassembled and bolts together on site. Flat furniture takes far less space to move than assembled furniture.</p></div><div class="row"><h3 class="disp">Reassemblable</h3><p>Joints must survive being taken apart and put back together many times, not once. A hotel can move, store or reconfigure its furniture.</p></div><div class="row"><h3 class="disp">Modular</h3><p>Each component can be replaced on its own. One design can take different materials and parts over time, like a system rather than a single object.</p></div><div class="row"><h3 class="disp">Honest material</h3><p>Grain, age, marks and imperfections stay visible. We want each piece to look like it has a story.</p></div></div>
</div></section>


<section id="heading"><div class="wrap split">
 <div><span class="label eyebrow muted">Where we're heading</span><h2 class="disp">Give back. Collaborate.</h2>
 <p class="prose" style="margin-top:24px">We're just getting started, and we have big plans. We haven't planted a forest yet, and we won't pretend we have. But here's where we're heading.</p><div class="lead-img"><figure class="fig"><img src="{{ 'chair-legs-sand.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Close-up of two dark teak chair legs standing in sand at the water&#x27;s edge, small waves behind" width="768" height="1024" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div>
 <div><div class="rows"><div class="row"><h3 class="disp">Give back</h3><p>We want to share what we build with the communities behind our furniture: the makers we work with and the places the wood comes from.</p></div></div>
 <div class="btns" style="margin-top:20px"><a class="btn" href="/pages/contact?type=collab">Work with us</a></div></div>
</div></section>





